                <pb facs="0729" n="717" sameAs="frus:frus1941v02/pg717"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/9907: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Germany</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Morris</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-04-12T16:00:00+02:00">April 12, 1941—4
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 6:50 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1415. The Berlin afternoon press publishes a brief military communiqué stating
                    that German troops have established contact with Italian forces north of Lake
                    Ochrida and a congratulatory telegram from Hitler to Mussolini has been
                    sent.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Morris</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
